CONTENT = "Implemented the customizable FizzBuzz engine in `src/lib.rs`.\n\n`Matcher<T>` wraps a boxed predicate plus its substitution word, accepting any `Fn(T) -> bool` and any `S: ToString`. `Fizzy<T>` collects matchers through the `add_matcher` builder and `apply` lazily maps an iterator: it concatenates the words of every matching rule, and falls back to the item's own formatting when nothing matches, so the result works for any `T: Copy + Display` rather than only integers.\n\n`fizz_buzz<T>()` builds the standard \"fizz\" then \"buzz\" rules generically over `T: Copy + Display + From<u8> + PartialEq + Rem<Output = T> + 'static`, comparing against `T::from(0u8)` so it works for `i32`, `u64`, and similar primitives. Because it is just a `Fizzy`, it works over infinite iterators and any other sequence, not only counting numbers.\n\n`cargo test` passes all 4 tests: the standard 1..=16 output, another numeric type, custom matchers producing concatenated words, and an infinite iterator."
